{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: the D5, D3 and D4 security documentation head at exact d938a684ad167829921ce179dbf7358ca71ba135, tree a20325a9e643cb7fb1e0ba831fe1c3d344e4c93c (review request f4cdaf6f, promise 19c409d3). This review binds the child implementation request 918ef6b1 (promise c3f9fed5) only; the parent d8512f74 stays open for D6 and SECURITY.md, and the R2 and R8 queue dispositions stay with the planner. It may land. Nothing in it is deployed or needs deploying.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-24-security-docs-partial.md (artifact f9223f1c), first and in full, then docs/security/settings.md, scripts/security-settings.mjs, scripts/security-settings.test.mjs, docs/security/definition-authors.md, docs/security/trust-boundaries.md, and the diffs of docs/README.md, docs/testing.md and package.json. The nine artifact events are exactly the nine paths changed against Main. The worktree /private/tmp/artroom-builder-security-docs-d3-d6-20261024 is clean at the head on branch builder/security-docs-d3-d6-20261024. The merge-base with Main is Main itself, e83a1ee5 (the R4/R10/R13 landing); the head is seven commits above it. The delta is 9 files, 1,621 insertions and 2 deletions.\n\nGate: ordinary gate 62839 ran at 56e82303 (tree 521bc687) and passed: eight stages exit 0 with 40 compiler invocations, Vitest 3,553 passed and 3 skipped across 499 files with 0 unhandled errors, Node 42 of 42 (the 39 retained cases plus the three new D3 cases), Counting 55 of 55, before and after checkpoints equal and clean, gatePassed and unchangedCheckpoint true in the raw result. The final head differs from the tested head in the implementation note only (git diff --name-only 56e82303 d938a684), so the gate carries under docs/testing.md:597; the two trees are 521bc687 (tested) and a20325a9 (final). The audit manifest (7 of 7 files verified by sha256, the stated 1,152 bytes and digest) and its input roster (71 rows, all verified) agree with the raw result.json and stdout.log, which I read directly. The link check receipt at the same head and tree reports 694 relative links and 0 broken. The D3 focused repair receipt has the stated 4,288 bytes and digest.\n\nConditions of 918ef6b1, each checked:\n1. D5 first, then D3 and D4 only: the commit order is D5 (c80c8597), D4 (337047d1), D3 (dca7c374), the checker repair (905c0fa6), reader references and testing guidance (7612fc34), the Main merge (56e82303) and the note. No other finding is touched.\n2. Parent open for D6 and SECURITY.md: the note says so, and no SECURITY.md or D6 text is in the head.\n3. No genesis-invariant closure before R2 lands: settings.md says the separate R2 continuation remains open and makes no \"no object before genesis\" claim; definition-authors.md claims nothing about it.\n4. Common predecessor landed first: the merge-base is the R4/R10/R13 landing.\n5. Exact-head review, affected validation and ordinary gate: this review, the three-case Node run and gate 62839.\n6. No builder deployment: none is claimed; no Worker source, configuration, setting or provider changed.\n\nWhat I checked in the content.\n- docs/security/settings.md. I ran the checker and its three tests once at the head: 3 of 3 pass in 27 seconds; the checker reports 121 deployment and name rows, 570 source reads and 9 configurations, matching the page's 37 grouped rows and 121 pairs. The generated lookup equals the canonical rows (the test asserts it). I spot-checked twelve semantic rows against source and each is as stated: DEPLOYMENT (readDeployment, 1 to 128 UTF-8 bytes), SESSION_SECRET (SECRET_BYTES 32), ARTIFACTS_CONFIG (4,096 characters), ARTIFACTS_NAMESPACE (default artroom-demo), GITHUB_CLEANUP_TOKENS (1 MiB), MCP_ENABLED (exact \"true\"), MCP_TOOL_ADDITIONS (1,024 characters, at most the generic tool-name count), SCOPE_INDEX_MODE (register or enforce, undefined is enforce), the four SERVING limits (MAX_LIMIT 1,000,000), GROW_BINDING (8,192 characters), ARCHIVE_RESTART_DIRECTIVE (8,192 bytes), SCREEN_HOSTS (32 records). The page states its limits plainly: no deployed values, no provider test, and a wired health state is syntax and binding only. The semantic text of the other rows rests on Root's independent source review e3bfd988, which the note cites; the checker proves enumeration and ownership, not semantics, and the page says so.\n- scripts/security-settings.mjs. It parses with rolldown's parser and never imports or evaluates a Worker. It follows static relative and workspace runtime imports from each configured entry, treats type-only imports as marker declarations only, and refuses rather than omits: dynamic import and require, dynamic environment lookup outside the sandbox's checked finite domain, environment escape to an unrecognized callee, mutable or rest aliases, environment spread into arguments, and forwarding to a parameter not typed as an environment shape. Deployment identity (name, main, kind) is checked against each configuration; an undocumented read or an undocumented configured binding fails; declared-unused rows must have a declaration and no reader. The two tripwires (the sandbox mappings function's exact text and the object.ts metric-environment adapter with its sole typed consumer) fail on any change to those texts, which the page and the note describe honestly as tripwires, not proofs.\n- scripts/security-settings.test.mjs proves each refusal with specimens and with real-source overrides: an undocumented read added to health.ts through an inherited environment interface, a changed adapter in object.ts, a renamed binding in apps/room/wrangler.jsonc, a wrong forwarding position; a documented addition passes; the sandbox domain, selector and construction changes each fail; the simulator's three settings stay separate from the sandbox file.\n- docs/security/trust-boundaries.md. I checked each configuration's statements against the wrangler files at this head: room (namespace artroom-demo, bucket artroom-application-content, dataset artroom_metrics_v1, empty APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS, no MCP opt-in variables, no cross-Worker script_name), grow (worker.grow.ts, DEPLOYMENT dap-grow-v1, the pinned register, the same three shared resources), lending (namespace dap-lending, no bucket, dataset, REGISTRIES or AGENTS), demo (namespace dap-demo, SCOPE_INDEX_MODE enforce, the shared dataset, no bucket), simulator (no Scope, Artifacts, R2, MCP or metrics bindings, workers_dev and preview off, a cron trigger, fetch answers 404), sandbox (ROOM, GROW and LENDING service entrypoints, empty default SCREEN_HOSTS, the rollout file mapping grow.inguz.space), and the two assets-only Workers. The finding 3.13 table matches the files.\n- docs/security/definition-authors.md. Every cited path exists; all six named test witnesses exist by their exact titles; the 21 guard forms listed are all named in validate/guards.ts; isExtents documents approvals 0 to 64 and names of 1 to 64 bytes; the two anchors resolve. The fail-open table's statements rest on the cited validator and evaluator files and witnesses; I checked the citations and witnesses, not every evaluator branch.\n- docs/README.md adds the security references section with four resolving links. docs/testing.md's new section is accurate: package.json runs the new file once, first in the Node list after Vitest, and the section states what the check does not prove.\n\nDocument checks at d938a684:\n- git diff --check from Main e83a1ee5 is clean;\n- check-commit-messages from e83a1ee5 reports 7 checked, 0 flagged;\n- section citations on an export report 1,877 resolved, 0 broken and 5 known unresolved; the citation script is unchanged;\n- relative links in the six changed Markdown files: 136 checked, 0 broken (my check), in addition to the builder's whole-tree 694 and 0;\n- merging the head into Main e83a1ee5 gives exactly its tree, a20325a9;\n- the note's \"review and delivery remain null\" is its dated report form, accepted as for the other heads today.\n\nArchitecture: an inventory keyed to source with a structural checker that fails closed on syntax it does not understand is the right shape for a settings reference; the canonical JSON block with a generated lookup keeps one source of truth, and the pages separate what the files establish from what only hosted evidence can. Right shape, and it leaves D6 and SECURITY.md to the parent.\n\nSecurity: the pages name secrets and never carry values; each states which claims need hosted evidence; the checker never evaluates Worker code, so running it cannot touch a binding or a provider. The definition-author page is the first place the fail-open forms are written down with their missing policy, which is the finding's purpose. No new entry point, setting or secret is introduced.\n\nSimplification, nonblocking:\n- The two text tripwires are brittle by design: any whitespace change to the sandbox mappings function or the object.ts adapter fails the checker until the tripwire is updated. Documented; acceptable for two sites.\n- rolldown/parseAst is now imported by five repository scripts, but rolldown is not a declared dependency of the root; it arrives through vite. Pre-existing practice, not introduced by this head. A devDependency pin would make the scripts' parser explicit.\n- The real-source inventory test adds about 27 seconds to npm test (one measured run here). Acceptable for what it proves.\n\nFindings: none blocking. Nothing to deploy. The planner's open items referenced by the note (R2 disposition 9edfd360, R8 queue ba280953, parent d8512f74) are unchanged by this approval.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f9223f1c1469acd35400140db98614c5e6ad3963","binding":"assigned","head":"d938a684ad167829921ce179dbf7358ca71ba135","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:19c409d32e532572f18610fea30d8927f720a61d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572